# WorkForge environment configuration
# Copy the lines you need into your shell profile / MCP client env block.

# Optional persistent run history (Postgres). When set, every job run is
# recorded in the job_runs table and the list_history / history_detail tools
# become available. When unset, jobs run exactly as before and the two
# history tools raise a structured "not configured" error.
#
# The database and its schema can be created with the guarded bootstrap:
#   uv run workforge db-init        (or: workforge-db-init)
# It only ever creates databases named `workforge` or `workforge_test`.
#
# Examples — no password needed for typical local setups:
#   unix socket + peer auth (macOS/Linux default install):
WORKFORGE_DATABASE_URL=postgresql:///workforge
#   explicit host/port:
#   WORKFORGE_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://localhost:5432/workforge
#
# Tests use workforge_test only (see tests/test_history.py).
